@ October 13, 2026

Here we go again...

This release is mainly for the brave Hyper-V users who fought kernel panics
since 26.7, which got fixed in 26.7.6 only to cause segmentation faults for
others.  Thanks all for testing and correcting the problem in FreeBSD!

The other reason are fixes in the new interfaces settings API so that it
more closely matches the behaviour of the legacy page.

Both the iPerf and the FRR plugin have been reworked substantially.  In case
of FRR please read the migration notes linked below before updating.

Here are the full patch notes:

o interfaces: add missing validation for "configurable" and "spoofmac" in new settings API
o interfaces: only store "dhcp6_norequest_dns" in DHCPv6 mode in new settings API
o interfaces: only store "track6-interface" in ID association / Track interface modes in new settings API
o interfaces: do not render "none" to configuration in new settings API
o interfaces: move promiscuous mode to advanced in new settings API
o interfaces: fix index into $todo for proper flag check during apply in new settings API
o interfaces: provide better option group labels to DeviceField
o interfaces: add proper local/remote IP support to PPPoE IPCP
o interfaces: move legacy apply cache to /var/lib/php/tmp
o firewall: destination NAT: fix typo in parseRdrRules() causing faulty rules not being disabled
o firewall: aliases: validate that port aliases always have content
o firewall: revert a clone rule change so that cloned rules to appear adjacent to the original rule again
o mvc: UidField: add isolated updateValue() for installer user
o ui: bootgrid: sync columnselect-input state with (un)setColumns
o ui: sync expanded state for selected submenus
o ui: close mobile menu when a menu entry opens another tab of the current page (contributed by Greelan)
o plugins: os-ddclient 1.33[1]
o plugins: os-frr 2.0[2]
o plugins: os-iperf 2.0[3]
o src: pf: send syncookies from the receiving thread
o src: hyperv: fix two regressions in previous upstream patch
o src: pcib: only apply ARI translation to the own secondary bus of a bridge
o src: ktls CBC decrypt: avoid creating zero length iovec entries
o src: route/fib_algo: respect immediate_sync in fd_ref_nhop
o src: route/fib_algo: fix FIB_ALGO without ROUTE_MPATH option
o src: sysctl: retire SYSCTL_NODE_CHILDREN()

Out of band hotfix for PHP CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619:

o ports: php 8.5.12[4]


Stay safe,
Your OPNsense team

